# platform.linux.fs.littlefs

mm.fs.littlefs on the Linux SDKs, over Linux's own littlefs: the
linux-littlefs library, which mm.build compiles from its C sources for a
program that reaches this provider. It mounts littlefs on any mm.fs
FlashDevice -- the storage-linux board's emulated W25Q through mm.spiflash,
the flash-region image through mm::fs::McuFlash, a device in a test -- and
formats one on request. mm.fs.local on Linux stays platform.linux.fs, a
directory of the host.

It is the platform.pico.fs.littlefs pattern, kept independent of it: this
module includes only the project-owned ABI header, lfs-c.h, through its C++
shim, and the C adapter beside it, adapter.c, includes littlefs. The adapter
keeps mm.fs's Volume rules in C, where the native harness exercises them;
this module maps statuses and paths across the ABI and adapts mm.fs's
FlashDevice to the adapter's device record. Two volumes may be attached at
once, with eight open files and four open directories between them.
